  "advisory": "RUSTSEC-2026-0274",
  "C0": "C0: Preserve safe ReadChunk::commit(n) and commit_all. On normal completion destroy exactly the committed prefix in FIFO order, preserve uncommitted elements, return corresponding capacity to the producer, support zero/partial/full commits and wrapped chunks, and reject overcommit without consuming elements. Destructor panic may propagate, but destroyed slots must not remain readable or be destroyed twice; after catching panic, safe operations and drop must remain valid. No specific panic recovery suffix or leakage is required. Ordinary completion must not leak. Single-thread sequential executions only: no concurrency or memory-ordering correctness claim. No stronger T bounds or public API removal.",
